{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Terah lived in [Gm]Ur of Chal[Bb]dees
Seventy [Eb]years he walked the [Bb]dust
He became the fa[Gm]ther of three [Bb]sons
Abram, [Eb]Nahor, and [F]Haran he trust[Gm]ed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Haran became the father of [Bb]Lot
Milcah [Eb]and Iscah came from [Bb]him
[F/A][Gm]He died in the land of his [Eb]birth
While his [Cm]father [F]Terah still [Gm]lived
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Haran in [Bb]Ur, where the family [F]stayed
Before the [Gm]journey to Ca[Eb]naan
His early [Bb]death, a turning [F]point
In the [Gm]history of the [F]patri[Eb]archs
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]Abram and Nahor took [Bb]wives
Sa[Eb]rai was the wife of Ab[Bb]ram [F/A]
[Gm]Milcah was the daughter of Ha[Eb]ran
Who [Cm7]was the [F]father of Milc[Gm]ah
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]The account of Terah [Bb]is told
[Eb]Haran became the father of [Bb]Lot
[F/A][Gm]He died in the land of his [Eb]birth
In [Cm]Ur [F]of the Chal[Gm]deans
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Haran in [Bb]Ur, where the family [F]stayed
Before the [Gm]journey to Ca[Eb]naan
{end_of_verse}

